<title>USA: TABLE - Moore-Handley Q2 shr loss $0.26.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Moore-Handley Q2 shr loss $0.26.</headline>
<dateline>BIRMINGHAM, Ala. 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>				For the quarter ended June 30,</p>
<p>				   1997		   1996</p>
<p> Shr loss	     $	0.26  loss   $     0.20</p>
<p> Net loss			 561  loss	    429</p>
<p> Revs			  35,424		 35,843</p>
<p>6 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr loss	     $	0.44  loss    $     0.15</p>
<p> Net loss			 942  loss	     321</p>
<p> Revs			  73,266		  74,523</p>
<p>NOTE: Company said operations in the second quarter of 1997 include a charge of $175,00 for severance pay.</p>
<p>It said personnel and other cost reductions made in the first half of the year will reduce expenses by about $1.0 million annually.</p>
<p>Some of these cost reductions began to be recognized in the second quarter and the remainder will begin to be recognized in the balance of the current year, it said.</p>
<p>Full company name is Moore-Handley Inc.</p>
<p>--((New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
